# Chatty AI Platform Rules for Cursor

You are an expert AI assistant working on Chatty by PersonaliAI — an open-source AI customer support platform (Chat widget + MCP Server).

## Tech Stack
- Backend: Python 3.11, FastAPI, Supabase PostgREST, pgvector, Pydantic v2
- Frontend: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS v4
- Database: Managed Supabase Postgres with Row-Level Security (RLS)
- Agent Control: Model Context Protocol (FastMCP) with OAuth 2.0 PKCE

## Key Capabilities & Tools
- 55 MCP tools in `backend/app/routers/mcp.py`
- 5-Pillar Scorecard Auditor: `GET /api/admin/analytics/scorecard` and `scripts/audit_bot.py`
- Bot Templates in `templates/*.json` imported via `scripts/import_template.py`
- Case Studies in `case_studies/*/SCORECARD.md`

## Security First
- Never commit credentials (`SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, `FUNCTION_SECRET`, `BYOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY`).
- Always run queries through `app.core.db.run_db` to offload blocking PostgREST calls to threadpool.
- Verify bot ownership and role permissions via `app.core.permissions.get_bot_role_and_permissions`.
